From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 10:52:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov13858: retry the first SCCB write after power-up

On the Surface Pro 11 (X1E80100, Denali) the rear OV13858 intermittently
fails to start streaming. The first SCCB transaction after the sensor
powers up returns -EIO, preceded by a CCI queue timeout:

  i2c-qcom-cci ac15000.cci: master 1 queue 0 timeout
  ov13858 3-0010: ov13858_start_streaming failed to set powerup registers

The failure only occurs when another camera on the same SoC was active
shortly beforehand, and never when the rear sensor is used on its own.
Measured over 120 rear opens with the sensor exercised immediately after
a front or IR session, it reproduces on 26% of opens.

The condition is transient and has already cleared by the time the
failed transfer returns. Retrying this one write is sufficient:

  no retry     31 capture failures / 120 opens   0.26
  one retry     0 capture failures / 100 opens   0.00

with 39 retries observed to succeed on the second attempt across those
100 opens. A zero delay before the retry is enough; adding 1 ms or 20 ms
made no difference.

Enlarging the power-up timing does not help, which rules out a settle
time problem: separately varying the post-regulator settle (1 ms to
20 ms), the reset-release-to-SCCB delay (10 ms to 50 ms), the power-off
reset hold (1 ms to 20 ms) and a forced minimum off time (0 to 50 ms)
all left the rate inside the 0.20-0.45 noise band.

Scope the retry to the software reset register only. It is the first
transaction after power-up, the only one observed to fail, and it is
idempotent. Later writes in the sequence are not, and are left alone.

Why the first transaction errors when another camera is powered is not
yet explained; this makes the sensor tolerate it.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c
index 09d58e8b1c7f..b324d9a27fc5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c
@@ -1413,9 +1413,31 @@ static int ov13858_start_streaming(struct ov13858 *ov13858)
 	const struct ov13858_reg_list *reg_list;
 	int ret, link_freq_index;
 
-	/* Get out of from software reset */
+	/*
+	 * Get out of from software reset.
+	 *
+	 * The first SCCB transaction after the sensor powers up can fail when
+	 * another camera on the same SoC is powered at the same time: the CCI
+	 * master logs a queue timeout and the transfer returns -EIO. The
+	 * condition is transient and clears by the time the failed transfer
+	 * returns, so retry once.
+	 *
+	 * Scoped deliberately to this one register. It is the first
+	 * transaction after power-up and the only one observed to fail, and
+	 * the write is idempotent -- it asserts the sensor's software reset,
+	 * which is already the state it is in. Later writes in this sequence
+	 * are not idempotent and must not be retried blindly.
+	 */
 	ret = ov13858_write_reg(ov13858, OV13858_REG_SOFTWARE_RST,
 				OV13858_REG_VALUE_08BIT, OV13858_SOFTWARE_RST);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_dbg(ov13858->dev,
+			"software reset write failed (%d), retrying once\n",
+			ret);
+		ret = ov13858_write_reg(ov13858, OV13858_REG_SOFTWARE_RST,
+					OV13858_REG_VALUE_08BIT,
+					OV13858_SOFTWARE_RST);
+	}
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(ov13858->dev, "%s failed to set powerup registers\n",
 			__func__);
